<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσηγ-έομαι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσᾱγ-</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσομαι,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσηγοῦ σὺ λαβὼν ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					647
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>bring in, introduce,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοιδάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					174
				</span></i>
			 (dub.); ofreligious rites, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.49
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημαγωγίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.21.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					11.50
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>introduce, propose,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν πεῖραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἀναδασμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					684e
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					38
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.148
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.140
				</span></i>
			,al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. περί τινος</span>
			<i>make a proposal</i> on a subject, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.170
			</span></i> : c. inf., <i>propose,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. τὴν αὐλητρίδα χαίρειν ἐᾶν</span>
			to let her go, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				176e
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cri.</u>
				48a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Publ.</u>
				16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦτο τὸ μάθημα, ὅτι καλὸν εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>La.</u>
					179e
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. ὅπως..</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Them.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσηγουμένου τινός</span>
			<i>at</i> his <i>proposal, on</i> his <i>motion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.76
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1451.6
			</span></i> (Messene, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσηγεῖσθαί τινι</span>
			<i>represent</i> to a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσηγεῖται.. τοῖς ἐν τέλει οὖσιν ὡς
					οὐ χρεών..</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.73
				</span></i>
			: hence, <i>advise, instruct,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοιαῦτα μέντοὐγὼ φρονεῖν τούτοισιν
					εἰσηγησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					972
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ϝεωτέροις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. τοῖς πολεμίοις ἃ χρὴ καταλαβεῖν
					τῶν χωρίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					14.35
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>relate, narrate, explain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					189d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγον τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					20d
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
